From 77809e628411ce80c92ea5f3e471e49259de7bee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Phase1 Draft (Claude, for Terhi review)" <draft@local>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 05:06:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] refactor(sim): RNG unification, rebased across the
 real-unit trigger contract -- one numpy Generator drives EVERY simulation
 draw when passed (Poisson counts, inverse-CDF uniforms, cell multinomial,
 sample_points, offspring counts, both trigger simulations), giving fully
 seed-reproducible simulate() for the first time, INCLUDING the pure-Hawkes
 background path whose sample_points draw was historically unseeded. Content
 is the withdrawn 2c patch 3 adapted to the real-unit _sim_offspring: the
 Generator now draws the REAL-unit spatial displacement directly (no internal
 draw, no box-span rescale) and the thinning goes through
 within_real_box_window -- the rebase conflicts were exactly the two prior
 semantics commits' regions (_sim_offspring body,
 Spatial_Symmetric_Gaussian.simulate_trigger) and were resolved by taking BOTH
 changes. Backward compatibility preserved: rng=None falls back to np.random
 (plus geopandas' unseeded sample_points) so legacy call sites keep working;
 user-defined triggers with the old simulate_trigger(pars) signature are
 detected by TypeError fallback and stay on np.random (Temporal_Exponential /
 Spatial_Symmetric_Gaussian gain an rng kwarg). Capture-based tests adapted
 via a Generator-subclass spy (a duck-typed wrapper fails inside geopandas'
 default_rng). New parametrized test: identically seeded fresh Generators
 produce byte-identical simulations for plain hawkes AND cox. Distribution
 preserved per config where rng semantics are unchanged; streams intentionally
 differ where draws moved onto the Generator (2b contract). Verified: 48/48
 (reproducibility test repeated, green twice); inference value+gradient pins
 bit-identical across all four pin configs; ruff clean.

